PASSMENU(1)

# NAME

passmenu - dmenu-based interface to pass

# SYNOPSIS

*passmenu* [*--type*] [_dmenu-args_ ...]

# DESCRIPTION

*passmenu* provides a *dmenu*(1)-based interface to *pass*(1), the
standard Unix password manager.
It allows quick retrieval of passwords without opening a terminal
window.

By default, the selected password is copied to the clipboard.
If the *--type* option is specified, the password is instead
typed directly using *xdotool*(1).

On systems running Wayland, *dmenu-wl* is used in place of *dmenu*(1),
and *ydotool* is used in place of *xdotool*(1).
Note that *ydotool* requires access to the *uinput* device; additional
udev rules or similar configuration may be necessary to grant non-root
users permission.

# SEE ALSO

*pass*(1),
*dmenu*(1),
*xdotool*(1)

